messages.content:
You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: C05
Scenario title: Weekly Shared Caregiving Schedule
Initial workflow description:
I work out next week's childcare arrangements with my family. When someone cannot make it, we find another arrangement and tell each other.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "Who are the family members involved in the caregiving schedule, and does each person have a fixed role (e.g., primary caregiver, backup) or does the role vary week to week?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "How do family members currently share their availability with you before you draft the schedule — for example, do they message you individually, fill in a shared calendar, or tell you verbally?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "On which day of the week does the scheduling process typically start, and by when does the final schedule need to be agreed upon?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "When someone says they cannot make their slot, what is the process for finding a replacement — do you contact other family members in a specific order, or is it whoever responds first?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "What happens if no family member is available to cover a slot after you have tried to find an alternative — is there a fallback option such as external childcare or postponing the activity?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "Once the schedule is finalized or updated, how is it shared with everyone — for example, sent as a message in a group chat, posted somewhere visible, or communicated individually?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Weekly Shared Caregiving Schedule with explicit responsibilities, decisions and recorded completion.",
  "actors": [
    "mother",
    "partner",
    "grandparent",
    "backup caregiver"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "shared family calendar",
    "care availability form",
    "family messaging app",
    "care assignment table"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "childcare hours",
    "adult availability",
    "work commitments",
    "backup availability"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "weekly care plan",
    "accepted assignments",
    "updated calendar",
    "change acknowledgment"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Collect adult availability for the coming week",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "List care periods outside childcare hours",
      "actor": "partner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Match each care period with an available adult",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Request explicit acceptance from assigned caregivers",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Find a replacement for an uncovered period",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Publish the agreed schedule in the shared calendar",
      "actor": "partner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Notify affected caregivers of any later change",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A8",
      "name": "Record acknowledgment of the revised assignment",
      "actor": "backup caregiver"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Is every required care period assigned to an available adult?",
      "branches": [
        "request confirmations",
        "seek an available replacement"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Has the assigned caregiver accepted the period?",
      "branches": [
        "publish the assignment",
        "keep it pending and contact the caregiver"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "uncovered care period",
    "overlapping adult commitments",
    "assignment not accepted",
    "last-minute caregiver cancellation"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A7",
      "to": "A8",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A2",
      "rationale": "Identify time periods requiring care from agreed schedules."
    },
    {
      "target": "A3",
      "rationale": "Suggest nonconflicting assignments for family review."
    },
    {
      "target": "A8",
      "rationale": "Track missing acknowledgment after a schedule change."
    }
  ],
  "operating_context": {
    "frequency": "schedule prepared every Sunday and updated when availability changes",
    "manual_effort": "Initial coordination takes about twenty minutes in this fictional household.",
    "data_availability": "Adults provide their availability voluntarily; the shared table records accepted versus pending assignments.",
    "integration_and_approval_constraints": "Software may suggest an assignment but cannot treat silence as acceptance or override a caregiver's availability."
  },
  "interpretation": "Activity dependencies describe the nominal sequence. Decision branches and exception descriptions qualify that sequence; this is not an executable BPMN model."
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}
